      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-133930",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/71/716be3363620a0be576096e37149ed310720a9be3794b5a9a850fe04bca5795a.png)\n\nJake is practicing his baseball batting. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the angle at which Jake hits the ball and the distance the ball travels (in feet). Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in the angle of contact is the only cause of an increase in the distance traveled.\n2. An increase in force the ball is struck is the only cause of an increase in the distance traveled.\n3. The angle of contact and the force the ball is struck are both factors that influence the distance traveled."
